# Cursor rules

**Before making any change, read and follow
`.claude/skills/cluster-development/SKILL.md`** — the authoritative workflow for
this cluster (also loaded by `.cursor/rules/cluster-development.mdc`,
`alwaysApply: true`). `CLAUDE.md` and `AGENTS.md` point at the same place.

The rules that must hold in every change, restated here because they are the
ones that cost real damage:

- NEVER push to the default branch — branch plus merge request, always, including
  one-line fixes. The deploy jobs and Flux act on it.
- NEVER commit secrets. Host tooling references
  {% if secrets_backend == 'onepassword' %}`op://{{ onepassword_vault }}/<item>/<field>`{% else %}the secrets backend{% endif %};
  workloads read a Secret produced by an `ExternalSecret`.
- NEVER `kubectl apply` or `helm upgrade` to deploy: Flux owns everything under
  `kubernetes/`. Preview with `task flux:lint`, deploy by merging.
- Kubernetes manifests carry NO site literals — domains, addresses and CIDRs
  arrive as `${cluster_...}` substitutions from the `cluster-config` ConfigMap.
- Versions are single-sourced in `ansible/inventories/prod/group_vars/all.yml`;
  run `task flux:sync-versions` after changing a pin and commit the result.
- Ansible roles live in the weisssrv.infra collection, not in this repo. A role
  change is a library change plus a pin bump.
- Run `task lint` before opening a merge request.
